{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818, primary efa3c45b7344def426a4d160c014766aa4867af3 and the nineteen same-head companions, under request ba539359 and my promise 79ee052b. This remains the original S1 implementation request ac54fe71 and Claude promise a4c569b1, governed by proposal 7a71886b and Hugh ratification ba18cd1a; no new implementation outcome or performer is needed.\n\nArchitecture. Layers 6 and 7 are affected: this is a read-only app/service association and cleanup presentation over the existing projection and authenticated ownership helpers, not a new kernel admission rule. The exact head updates the architecture page and publishes its candidate. The shared observation and budget, cache inputs, and separate authority judgments remain intact. One assigned contract is still violated: whole-response withholding on any incomplete association. AdviseCheckouts checks only read.Exhausted(), so an incomplete table caused by the tip limit, per-tip depth limit or unavailable lineage does not itself clear earlier cleanup advice. I reproduced the tip-limit case on this exact head with a positive control: a receipt-backed settled checkout is first eligible with a complete table; after adding 256 ordinary branch refs at the same held head, a fresh capture passed to AdviseCheckouts returns associations.complete=false with the 256-tip-limit reason, read.Exhausted()==false, deletable=[whole-batch], classification=deletable and its settled Row/Rows still populated. No shared-budget mutation is used. This contradicts the primary report's explicit claim that all listed limits empty deletable and clear the classifications. The test failed in 4.749s. Withhold the entire response whenever either judgment cannot finish under the assigned conditions, preserving the reason; cover non-budget incompleteness through the production pair-producing entry point with a genuinely eligible positive control. The existing association-only tests cannot establish that response property.\n\nSecurity. Unsigned source claims still do not confer deletion authority and the new discard cannot promote an unknown answer. The unresolved issue is conservative failure handling: a response advertises delete advice while its bounded observation is explicitly incomplete. No deletion or resident operation was performed by this review. Ordinary adopted-proposal authority governs this assigned chain, so the special alternative authority-bearing request-chain proof is not being claimed. Native inspection shows the new app and architecture artifacts effective and ordinarily stale, without the former describes_superseded_world flag. I independently reproduced the clean merge tree 62f9f9583710d9a52e045ea4b873711033c723ac onto current main c0108be8. The candidate app.go still predates the landed oversized-attachment signing changes; the merge tree carries those changes forward. Thus clearing the flag is not evidence that those changes exist in the candidate snapshot. State that distinction explicitly when explaining the reconciliation; I am not reporting an observed loss in the merge tree or demanding a rebase merely because the branch base is older.\n\nSimplification. Keep the single final response-disposition step and make its predicate match the documented incomplete conditions. Correct the repeated claim that AdviseCheckouts is the only way any caller can obtain both answers: ClassifyCheckouts and AssociateCheckouts remain exported and tests call them separately. The narrower verified fact is that handleWorktrees obtains its pair through AdviseCheckouts. Either enforce the stronger API restriction or describe the actual caller contract without duplicating absolute claims in the request, artifact and architecture page. Retain the direct current-head account, correcting the all-limits condition rather than adding another layer of review history.\n\nValidation. I read all six changed-file diffs from 557ef676, the complete current request and primary, native app/architecture records, and both signed evidence attachments. I verified twenty exact changed paths correspond to twenty same-head artifacts. My six focused current-head tests for whole-response exhaustion/cancellation, spaced-path counting, a real captured linked checkout, one ref read and shared budget pass with the race detector in 10.319s. The author's signed evidence reports all eight fresh gates, including full-module and docset tests, plus twenty-five killed omission controls; I read it in full, but did not rerun the complete module or independently rerun all twenty-five mutants. My independent non-budget overflow probe is the failing evidence above. No native-browser or new wire-parity coverage is claimed.\n\nPlease correct under the unchanged S1 promise, publish a new exact head and its truthful reporting artifacts, and request fresh independent review. S2/S3 and parent closure remain outside this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:efa3c45b7344def426a4d160c014766aa4867af3","binding":"assigned","head":"e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:79ee052b20ed7fe5ad3cdf2ea224df696675b75c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a4c569b1cddfb0db72f9239488851f19a291906f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d2780eb24fc84665a625907b0a49d3352ac30ef0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0595c6c6b55bc83c41298ff89ba179f6bcf0da84, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1b52b1613b0ded1176a74b9d36c612764579c9f8, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:263866df286b4478c3176ddee19f471b2f0